{
  "analysis": "I have confirmed the toolchain and VM loading mechanism. Before attempting a full Doom build, I should verify the VM's run loop, syscall entry, and instruction support, especially branch delay slots and multiply/divide, because compiler-generated MIPS code may use instructions the VM does not support. A small test program will validate the toolchain+VM path efficiently.",
  "plan": "Inspect vm.js runProgram, syscall entry, SPECIAL dispatch, stores, jumps, multiply/divide, and branch handling. Then compile and run a tiny MIPS test program that writes to stdout and loops, to validate the toolchain and VM before building Doom.",
